{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And likewise you shall do to your maidservant.</b> This does not refer back to the boring of the ear, for there is no boring of the ear for a woman; rather, it refers back to the gifts (הענקה). And like it is (Exodus 21:11): ״ואם שלש אלה״ — which does not refer back to the matter of food, clothing, and conjugal rights mentioned just before it, but rather to ״אשר יעדה והפדה״ — to be designated in marriage or redeemed. And likewise again (Exodus 22:2 [MT 21:37]): ״אם זרחה השמש עליו״ and so on, which refers back to ״חמשה בקר ישלם״ — he shall pay five cattle."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:48:26.718629885Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}